A R2,4 million Sea Point apartment – described as an “expensive jail cell” – has set tongues wagging on social media.

SEA POINT APARTMENT LEAVES SOCIAL MEDIA SHOCKED

On the X app, entrepreneur Koshiek Karan posted a screenshot of a listing for a Sea Point apartment priced at R2,4 million.

The 18 m² property – the size of a single garage – was located in a trendy apartment block on the corner of Main and Bellevue Roads.



It featured 0.5 bedrooms and one bathroom, and judging by the pictures, it was a tight squeeze.

Karan tweeted: “Arrest everyone!”

His followers agreed at the absurdity of both the price and size.

@slap__tjips: “R2.45m for 18 square is insanity”

@Tom_Ziege: “What is a 0.5 bedroom? Half a bedroom? Or room for only half a bed?”

@Thando654321: “Daylight robbery. This is a heist”.



@SantanaGP: “No man, Cape Town, even for you, this is a stretch. Why does the city approve such things?”

For others, it was nothing new for Sea Point …

@mrs_milli00n: “The target market will purchase without blinking twice🤣“

@TechChiefsZA: “I think it’s fair. After buying this, how much do you rent it out for? 2k a night”

A studio apartment in Sea Point is going viral for all the wrong reasons. Images: Private Property

QUIRKY OR BIZARRE?

With the growing demand for property in Cape Town, particularly in areas like Sea Point and the Atlantic Seaboard, many landlords are getting bang for their buck by leasing out any available space.

One TikToker has revealed a look inside his rental, a bachelor pad in an apartment building, that requires a trap door to get in!

Another TikToker documented how she was forced to move into the attic of her rental building to save money.

In another post, a studio apartment described as a “shoebox” was listed at a whopping R3,6 million!
